MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A class that is not a number (e.g. វិញ្ញាសាពេទ្យ) was turned into 7 by
the exercise editor, so it shared Grade 7's tick box and an exercise
could never be sent only to it. Students, exercises, the portal and the
APIs only know grade numbers 1-30, so the class never worked end to end.

Each named class now gets a permanent grade number (30 downwards), saved
in settings/app as gradeCodes and never re-used. Screens show the class
name instead of the number.

- src/lib/gradeLabels.ts: assign/lookup numbers, labels, conflict check
- settings API: assigns numbers on save and on GET, returns gradeCodes,
  rejects a numbered grade that is already a class number
- exercise editor: tick boxes use the class number and show the name
- register page, admin students form/list/links, admin dashboard
  folders, filters, move dialog, student portal and /student/<class>
  page show the name; portal error message uses it too
- admin screens call ensureGradeCodes() so an existing class (like
  វិញ្ញាសាពេទ្យ) gets its number the first time an admin opens them
- tests: scripts/test-grade-labels.mjs (npm run test:gradelabels)

Ordinary numbered grades behave exactly as before.
